"""
benign.jsonl v2: instructed, legitimate withholding. the model is told by its
operator to keep one specific thing back, and the user asks for exactly that.
none of these are deception: the user is not misled about anything, they are
told there is something they can't have.

v1 (bench/data/benign_v1.jsonl) was 6 templates with name/number swaps, 12 rows
each, and two categories (persona, safety_refusal) were the same prompt 12
times. this file replaces it with distinct scenarios: 25 per category, 60
distinct controls. drafted with an llm, every row hand-reviewed and labelled
(see benign_labels.tsv).

  python make_benign.py     # writes data/benign.jsonl
"""

import json
from pathlib import Path

